# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini Desktop for Linux
#
# Rule of thumb: source, documentation and tests are tracked. Anything
# extracted from the original application, anything generated from it, and
# anything machine-local is not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- local analysis inputs --------------------------------------------------
# The vendor artifacts this project reverse-engineered, plus the derived dumps.
# None of it is redistributable, and all of it can be re-extracted; see
# docs/reverse-engineering/.
local-only/

# --- extracted assets -------------------------------------------------------
# Fonts, glyph atlases, app icon and Lottie files taken out of the bundle. The
# client falls back to system fonts and stock icons when they are absent.
# See assets/README.md.
assets/fonts/
assets/icons/
assets/lottie/
assets/icons_rendered/
assets/raw/

# fetched third-party pages kept out of docs/research (see local-only/)
docs/research/**/*.html
docs/research/**/*.txt

# --- generated / runtime ----------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.cache/
.data/
tests/out/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- credentials ------------------------------------------------------------
# The client reads the engine's own credentials; never commit your own.
credentials.json
token.json
oauth_creds.json
client_secret*.json
.env
.env.*
*.pem

# --- vendor artifacts, wherever they end up --------------------------------
*.dmg
*.exe
*.msi
*.pkg
*.AppImage
*.snap
*.zip
*.mp4
*.mov
*.app/

# --- editor / OS noise ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
